id: pm-slack-i7ug
title: Install the pinned release npm into a job-local prefix
description: "The release workflow replaces the runner's global npm with the pinned npm. Parallel jobs on one runner host share the toolcache Node installation, so one job's global install mutates a sibling job's npm mid-install (ENOTEMPTY, or npm: command not found), as reported by unbraind/pm-ops#284 for the fleet."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ops#284","gh:unbraind/pm-slack#206"
created_at: "2026-11-16T14:42:01.458Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T10:25:46.644Z"
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: The release workflow installs the pinned npm with --prefix into a job-local directory and prepends that prefix bin to the job path; The workflow keeps the exact-version assertion on the effective npm; A workflow-contract test fails if any workflow replaces the global npm
comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T14:45:44.306Z",pi-glm,"Root cause (fleet-wide, reported as unbraind/pm-ops#284): after setup-node, every deep and release job ran a global npm install of the pinned npm. On the shared local runners, all containers on one host share the toolcache Node installation mounted at the runner tool directory, so parallel jobs replaced the same npm and siblings failed with ENOTEMPTY (exit 217) or npm: command not found (exit 127). Fix: the release workflow installs the pinned npm into a job-local prefix and prepends that prefix bin to the job path, keeping the exact-version assertion on the effective npm. Contract updates: the pinned-bootstrap step assertions require the prefix form, only the install step itself may prepend to the job path, and a new workflow-wide audit fails if any workflow replaces the global npm. Gates: typecheck, the full quick tier (1028 tests) and changelog:check all pass on this branch."
  "2026-11-16T15:17:47.518Z",codex-sol,"Continuation: verified the existing worktree and remote branch state, preserved the earlier changes, and reused this item. Rerunning required gates to completion under the continuation author before committing results."
  "2026-11-16T15:30:07.206Z",codex-sol,"Continuation review adds a separate next-step exact-version assertion and explicit ignore-scripts/no-audit/no-fund flags. The workflow-wide regression now also rejects global npm replacement with flags between --global and npm@. This extends the existing pushed implementation without creating a duplicate pull request. The repository defines no lint script; its existing docstring gate is included alongside typecheck, quick tests, workflow contracts and changelog verification."
  "2026-11-16T15:42:12.372Z",codex-sol,The first combined gate command hit its 20-minute timeout during shared-host disk contention and is not pass evidence. Retrying all gates to completion using memory-backed temporary fixtures and the existing harness deadline scale. Assertions and test selection are unchanged.
  "2026-11-16T16:07:39.556Z",codex-sol,"Typecheck and the existing docstring static gate passed; this package has no lint script. All 12 workflow-contract tests passed. Refreshed tags include the intervening canonical release, so regenerated changelog bytes retain that canonical section. Initial broad quick tests timed out; replacement broad gates and the wrapped changelog check remain pending."
  "2026-11-16T16:11:59.183Z",codex-sol,"Implementation commit 7374fbd46d45fd2f25d5de292983b555f7576844 contains the requested fix and package-owned regression contracts. Focused contracts and changelog verification passed; typecheck and lint or the existing docstring static gate passed. The first broad quick attempt timed out, and its replacement remains active. The shared runner dispatch hold is respected before publication. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-16T16:17:59.029Z",codex-sol,"Complete local gate rerun passed: npm run typecheck && npm run docstring && npm test && node --test test/release-workflow.test.ts && npm run changelog:check && git diff --check, with PM_TEST_DEPTH=quick and the existing deadline scale. The complete quick suite passed, and all 12 workflow-contract tests passed. The earlier timeout is superseded by this completed run. This package has no lint script; the existing docstring static gate passed. Exact-head remote CI remains pending the shared dispatch hold."
  "2026-11-16T16:38:12.957Z",codex-sol,Linked the generated changelog refresh retained from the intervening canonical release. The complete local gate chain and wrapped changelog check passed; remote CI for the published branch is queued.
  "2026-11-16T19:00:07.012Z",codex,"2026-11-16 19:2xZ (orchestrator): main gained #199 (pinned reusable Daily Release), which removed the vendored release job and with it the only global npm install in this repo. Merged origin/main into fix/job-local-npm: release.yml and test/release-workflow.test.ts now equal main's, plus one guard test that fails if any workflow replaces the global npm (proved: a probe workflow with 'npm install --global npm@11.21.0' fails it). The job-local install for the shared release flow lands through pm-ops#289. Gates: node --test test/release-workflow.test.ts 7/7, typecheck, docstring, changelog:check exit 0."
  "2026-11-16T19:23:59.881Z",codex-sol,"Review round P: replace the workflow-wide regex with a dependency-free shell command parser and regression fixtures. Parse run scripts with existing yaml where available; preserve allowed prefix-local installs. Verify typecheck, lint or docstring, focused guard/workflow contracts and changelog checks before pushing. No review-thread actions."
  "2026-11-16T19:28:39.817Z",codex-sol,"Review round P addresses PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM63-6kV and PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64FokT: shared-npm replacement guard now tokenizes shell commands and uses existing yaml for run scripts. Added 38 fixtures covering npm aliases, flag placement/location, package specs, continuations, quotes/paths, separators and allowed installs. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and npm run changelog:check PASS. The new linked guard and workflow contracts passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress: 45 pass, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo. Full-suite certification is left to CI; review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-17T01:51:22.985Z",codex-sol,"Review round AA: pulled and verified the open PR head. Source inspection confirms the reported guard gaps. Replace shell tokenization with conservative logical-line matching and step-only script extraction, with intended false positives and regression fixtures."
  "2026-11-17T01:58:36.216Z",codex-sol,Typecheck and test compilation passed. This package has no lint script; attempting its installed pm-ops ESLint export failed because the optional @babel/eslint-parser peer is absent. No dependencies added. Running the remaining configured gates separately; lint remains unavailable in this package.
  "2026-11-17T02:02:13.658Z",codex-sol,"All five scoped threads verified valid: PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64GLjd, PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64LiA3, PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64LiBA, PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64LiBI, PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64LiBN. Replaced the tokenizer with conservative logical-line matching; the existing direct YAML dependency now collects only jobs.*.steps[*].run. Guard plus release-workflow suite: 60 passed, including all real workflows. Typecheck, test compilation and changelog:check passed. No duplication script is configured. Changed-file lint passed using the already installed shared pm-ops policy; AA_ESLINT_MODULE selects its complete installed module because this package has no lint script and lacks the optional local parser peer. No dependencies added; no findings refused. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T03:38:09.549Z",pi-claude,"Round AF follow-up on the fail-closed guard, from the pm-ado review threads PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864PGRG and PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864P73_ and the identical pm-lint threads PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn2, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn6 and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn7; this repository carries the same guard with the direct YAML dependency. All three findings were reproduced against the guard source first: a prefix bootstrap followed by '&& npm install -g npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0' and step env NPM_CONFIG_GLOBAL=true were all accepted by the previous code.\n\n1. Segment-scoped prefix exception: run scripts now split into command segments at unquoted ;, &, | and newlines. The scanner tracks quote state across lines and $( … ) substitutions (which nest a fresh quoting context even inside double quotes), skips comments and here-document bodies, and any script that cannot be delimited (unbalanced quote or substitution) fails closed as 'undelimitable command line'. The job-local prefix exception only covers the segment carrying it; rejected fixtures add 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-11.19.0\" npm@11.19.0 && npm install -g npm@11.19.0' and 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-local\" npm@11.19.0; npm install -g npm@11.19.0'. Approved bootstrap fixtures stay accepted.\n2. Combined short flags: any single-dash letter cluster containing g now marks global (rejected: 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -dg npm@11.19.0'); 'npm install -D pnpm' and 'npm install -gpld pnpm' stay accepted.\n3. Workflow, job and step env compose for each step run, the step scope taking precedence; npm reads npm_config_* keys case-insensitively. npm_config_global set to anything other than false/0/empty, npm_config_location=global, a ${{ … }} expression value, or an unreadable env scope or entry forces every npm install in that run global unless its own segment carries a job-local prefix. Fixtures cover step env flow mapping, job env flow and block styles, workflow env, expression values, location=global, step-override (job \"true\" + step \"false\" accepted) and accepted \"false\"/\"0\"/\"\" values.\n\nGates: guard suite 62 passed; release-workflow suite 7 passed; typecheck, test build and changelog:check passed (this package configures no lint or duplication script). Every workflow in the repository still scans clean. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T05:22:27.993Z",codex-sol,"Round AH: implement conservative run-wide global configuration and markers, install-family aliases, redirect-safe prefix segmentation, and comment-free effective prefix exemptions. Preserve all existing rejected fixtures and approved bootstrap workflows; verify required package gates before releasing the claim. No review-thread mutations."
  "2026-11-17T05:29:49.816Z",codex-sol,"Round AH verification: 109 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips (102 guard fixtures plus release-workflow contracts). npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run docstring, npm run changelog:check and git diff --check all passed. No lint or duplication scripts exist. Threads PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64QHNG, PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64QHNQ, PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64QnL6 and PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64QnMA are addressed by this change. All earlier rejected fixtures are retained; approved bootstraps and repository workflows pass. Global signals are run-wide, and only effective command arguments can establish a prefix exemption. Shared guard logic matches all four copies. Protected item dates are unchanged. Exact-head CI remains pending; no thread actions, publishing or merges."
  "2026-11-17T07:46:29.140Z",pi-guard-1117aj,"Round AJ: replaced the guard's per-segment shell parser with a line-based fail-closed rule, identical to the other fleet repositories: logical lines only (continuations joined, newline-only splits), comment and here-document text scanned like any other text, install family extended with update/up/upgrade/udpate, markers covering single-dash g clusters, global-containing tokens, -L with any value and two-plus-letter prefixes of global/location, npm config set/set as a run-wide global signal (narrowed to a set token: a read-only 'npm config get globalconfig' line tripped the broader form), operands naming npm by substring or computed form (tarball URLs, x@npm:npm), exemptions restricted to exact approved bootstrap lines, and step-level rejection of GITHUB_ENV npm_config_* writes and global/location npmrc writes. The hand-rolled workflow extractor now consumes inert job-level sequence values such as needs lists, so the guard stays dependency-free across the fleet."
  "2026-11-17T08:23:21.752Z",codex-sol,"Round AM verified against unchanged guard: punctuation and comment-continuation bypasses, operandless global installs, persistent npm config setters, and spaced YAML env keys reproduce. Quoted command words already reject; add explicit regression coverage. Keep line-based checks and exact raw-line bootstrap matching. Unresolved review threads: PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64Us6C. Delegated npx finding is already rejected by Round AJ; preserve its rejected fixture. Run targeted gates directly; never execute linked PM tests. Preserve the existing test-session isolation import in the pm-vcs fixture."
  "2026-11-17T08:29:10.048Z",codex-sol,"Round AM targeted verification: 160 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts => PASS; npm run typecheck => PASS; npm run changelog:check => PASS. Scripts absent: lint, duplicates. All real workflows pass the guard; no bootstrap trailing comment was found. Guard source md5 d7ec9edd85b0c9fbe3d5a9f0e4d8d9e2 is identical across five packages. Fixture bodies match, retaining the required pm-vcs session-isolation import. Protected root item dates are unchanged; rejected fixtures are preserved. Same-class config persistence and spaced YAML env-key fixes from PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGg, PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64U3xi and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGj were applied to every copy. Full-suite certification remains with CI. Releasing this claim without closing the item."
  "2026-11-17T08:42:18.643Z",codex-sol,"Round AN: inspect unresolved review threads; scan joined and physical lines independently and union findings, with exact bootstrap exemptions local to each form. Preserve all fixtures and add quoted-hash regressions. Run the requested package gates directly; do not execute linked PM tests."
  "2026-11-17T08:44:29.999Z",codex-sol,"Unimplemented outside Round AN: PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64Vsdx, option values and redirect filenames hide operandless global updates. Both examples still reproduce after the continuation union; tracked separately in pm-slack-global-update-operands because changing operand classification needs a distinct policy and fixtures."
  "2026-11-17T08:46:59.635Z",codex-sol,"Round AN verified: PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64Vsdp. Joined and physical scans union findings; exact bootstrap exemptions apply per form. All old fixtures retained; four quoted-hash cases plus LF/CRLF union/exemption/dedup checks added. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts: 165/165 pass, zero skipped. npm run typecheck and npm run changelog:check: pass. No lint or duplicate npm script exists. Guard md5: 9472ab1dff99c26c27085f766054f46d. Review threads were read only; lifecycle timestamps preserved."
  "2026-11-17T09:01:55.966Z",codex-sol,"Round AP: reject every global update/up/upgrade/udpate line regardless of operands; option values, redirect targets and comment words cannot hide an update. Install-family operand handling stays unchanged. Preserve all prior fixtures, add the five requested rejections and alias/global-environment coverage, then run the Round AN gates directly. All five PRs remain open. No review-thread mutations."
  "2026-11-17T09:03:04.669Z",codex-sol,"Round AP verification: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts => PASS; npm run typecheck => PASS; npm run changelog:check => PASS; git diff --check => PASS. Focused suite: ℹ tests 171, ℹ pass 171, ℹ fail 0, ℹ cancelled 0, ℹ skipped 0, ℹ todo 0. Every real workflow still passes; all prior fixtures retained. Guard md5 e882f7b9396d4a810ccf85250dc05a04. No configured lint, duplicates script."
  "2026-11-17T10:20:50.579Z",codex-sol,"Round AR: reproduced assignment-valued short-flag, renamed-archive, quoted-expression and uppercase Boolean bypasses against the unchanged shared guard. Preserve dual line scans and all fixtures; replace global operand inference with a registry-spec allowlist, normalize option names before marker tests and compare env values exactly. Run the round AN gates and regenerate changelog after all tracker writes. Leave this item open."
  "2026-11-17T10:25:45.513Z",codex-sol,"Round AR implementation and validation: PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64YB_f and PRRT_kwDOSYpJkM64YB_o. Global install operands now require the plain registry name-spec allowlist and exclude npm identities; archive, path, URL, git, alias, computed and quote-fragment operands reject. Option names are unquoted and split before assignment-valued marker tests. Env keys ignore case but safe global/location values compare exactly, including run assignments. Both physical and joined scans and bootstrap exemptions remain. Preserved all prior fixtures; focused guard: 202/202; round AN contract gate: 209/209; typecheck passed. All real workflows pass the guard. Guard md5: 1b36b35bf3ce5df79ae313b939f17971. Merging origin/main; only CHANGELOG.md conflicted. Selected main before regeneration; verify every published section retains its main-branch bullets before committing the merge. Final tracker writes precede tag refresh and changelog regeneration/check; keep the item in_progress and release the claim. No review thread mutations or workflow dispatches."
